  "details": "I'd like to have variables that I can add to my status, so people can always see them updated in game. Below are a few examples.\n\n`My local time is {UTC+2} right now`\n\nThis would also allow to announce meetings in relative time, like in discord!\n\n`Available until {<t:1689408600:R>} today`\n\nThis could allow you to expose the current world you are in, without exposing the instance if you want people to request an invite first.\n\n`I'm in {WORLD_NAME} right now, please request an invite`\n\nBonus points if you can make it dynamic, so the status changes automatically based on a condition, e.g. by time or world ID. Below are examples with if/else in the short C# format `condition ? resultIfTrue : resultIfFalse`\n\n`{UTC+3 > \"23:30\" ? \"Sleeping, please do not disturb\" : \"Feel free to join me right now!\" }`\n\n`{WORLD_NAME == \"Movie World\" ? \"Busy watching a movie\" : \"Feel free to join me right now!\" }`",
